{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much","id":1532080,"title":"a way for a MTA and DTF crossover without changing the lore if either game too much?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-06T07:40:41-08:00","id":1532080,"title":"a way for a MTA and DTF crossover without changing the lore if either game too much?","content":"Hi guys. So, Mage: The Ascension bas a lot of demons and they're very different from the protagonists of Demon the Fallen. I wanted to know how to do shared setting between the two games, without changing the setting of either game too much. what is your suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T08:04:57-08:00","id":1532082,"title":"","content":"My basic concept is a common foe. The Umbrood (and Demons are a type of Umbrood) are complex one offs by definition. The common foe brings the two groups together focusing on the story and the problem rather than the metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T08:32:48-08:00","id":1532083,"title":"","content":"The lore of the two games are fully compatible, as is. In particular, the lore for <b>DtF</b> is that in prehistory, reality was multiple choice, in a manner not unlike the Fractured Cosmos described in <b>Time of Judgment: Ascension</b>. But some time between when the demons got locked up in the Abyss eons ago and when they got released from the Abyss very recently, that multiple choice nature of reality got lost; and the current version of reality is singular. <b>MtA</b> assumes, by default, that the nature of reality is singular, but mutable; if it was ever multiple choice, that was a <i>long</i> time ago, long before any of the events that have shaped their lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:30:49-08:00","id":1532096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532082#post1532082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My basic concept is a common foe. The Umbrood (and Demons are a type of Umbrood) are complex one offs by definition. The common foe brings the two groups together focusing on the story and the problem rather than the metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait,demons are a type of Umbrood? I thought they were a distinct separate being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-06-2024, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:31:58-08:00","id":1532097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532083#post1532083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lore of the two games are fully compatible, as is. In particular, the lore for <b>DtF</b> is that in prehistory, reality was multiple choice, in a manner not unlike the Fractured Cosmos described in <b>Time of Judgment: Ascension</b>. But some time between when the demons got locked up in the Abyss eons ago and when they got released from the Abyss very recently, that multiple choice nature of reality got lost; and the current version of reality is singular. <b>MtA</b> assumes, by default, that the nature of reality is singular, but mutable; if it was ever multiple choice, that was a <i>long</i> time ago, long before any of the events that have shaped their lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you expand on that if you don't mind? What does the Fractured Cosmos look from the perspective of Mages? I haven't read Time of Judgement: Ascension unfortunately","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:41:06-08:00","id":1532099,"title":"","content":"Also I want to clarify that I am not planning to run a crossover game any time soon,I just don't have the time currently<br /> but I wanted know how the two settings would mesh together","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:13:41-08:00","id":1532103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532096#post1532096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait,demons are a type of Umbrood? I thought they were a distinct separate being?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a distinct splat. But Umbroods cover an incredibly wide range. The rules for making Umbroods are meant to cover a vast range of types with simplicity. <br /> <br /> Mages would see Demons, Faeries, Djinni, Angels, and so many more types as types of Umbroods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:30:09-08:00","id":1532106,"title":"","content":"I would contest that last part. Mages are generally aware that human labels are wildly imperfect. Words like &quot;demon&quot; covers Umbrood, Bygones, Avatars, and other entities that don't even fit within the more expansive ability for mages to classify things. While certainly some mages are tempted to cluster lots of things under the large umbrella that is &quot;Umbrood,&quot; the fact that many of them can't be bound with mastery of Spirit alone undermines such a mono-focused idea. This is even more true when you get into the weeds with concepts like the idea that entities that did not being as Umbrood can partially or fully become spirits if in the Umbra for too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T17:44:34-08:00","id":1532130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532097#post1532097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you expand on that if you don't mind? What does the Fractured Cosmos look from the perspective of Mages? I haven't read Time of Judgement: Ascension unfortunately</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fractured Cosmos is the idea that the World of Darkness exists as multiple parallel realities that echo each other. The DtF version of this idea talks about how various contradictory origin stories of the universe are all simultaneously true, but take place on different levels of reality. On one level, the universe came into existence billions of years ago and developed through natural processes into what it is now; on another layer, it was created by God over the course of six days approximately 6000 years ago. Both versions are true, on their respective layers. But all of that multiplicity has been lost, and reality now only has one layer. <br /> <br /> The version described in ToJ:Ascension basically says that every gameline has its own layer of reality, with the Vampire-based layer operating according to the metaphysics of Vampire; the Werewolf-based layer operating according to the metaphysics of Werewolf, and so on. The book <i>doesn't</i> say that \u201cthis is the Truth of the World of Darkness\u201d; but it <i>does</i> say that it's a possibility if Storytellers want to explore it. Basically, it's a Shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T18:21:15-08:00","id":1532132,"title":"","content":"Cool,very nice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:55:20-08:00","id":1532192,"title":"","content":"Besides all that Dataweaver has already explained, if you want to truly tie in the 2 lores into a cohesive and neat idea, it is very simple: the Fallen were created by the Demiurge, as per in their lore, they revolt, fought against it, lost and were bounded into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Cool so far.<br /> <br /> Lucifer then finds out something amazing about humanity, and wants to protect it.<br /> <br /> What is it that Lucifer found so astonishing about humanity? DtF never says.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> You see, Mage the Ascension has the idea of &quot;The One&quot; and that the &quot;Avatars&quot; are &quot;fragments of the One&quot;.<br /> <br /> Getting my meaning yet?<br /> <br /> Yes, God (or the Demiurge or whatever) &quot;died&quot;, and its soul got divided into endless (maybe even infinite?) fragments that Mages call as &quot;Avatars&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the &quot;Demons&quot; are the Fallen Angels created by God, but humans are pieces of the &quot;God's soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> That would explain the Mages' ability to &quot;alter reality&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's also the most Gnostic view possible that is almost unapologetically described in almost all WoD games, therefore it would be more than fitting for a &quot;unifying lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, maybe in keeping that trend, what Lucifer knows and what he really wants (and has never told anybody) is to &quot;prop up humanity&quot; (or, as the Mages call it, ASCENSION) and by doing that, &quot;resurrecting&quot; God.<br /> <br /> This is Gnosticism 101 by the way. Under Gnosticism, we (in the real world) we are all GOD, but we forgot that we are God and we just need to &quot;remember&quot; that we are God; each one of us hold a shard of &quot;God's soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea of Gnosticism is very much like Ascension, but for Gnosticism it is necessary a sort of &quot;global Ascension&quot; not unlike what the Technocracy believes, because for Gnosticism &quot;God&quot; will only be &quot;revived&quot; once all of us &quot;remember&quot; that we are actually &quot;God&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, for Gnosticism, the material world was created by the &quot;Demiurge&quot;, which is a false &quot;God&quot; (that coincidentally is the God of the Bible) that created the material world as a prison for the shards of God, so that we couldn't remember that we are God (yes, Gnosticism is also &quot;Matrix&quot; in essence).<br /> <br /> So there you have, if you want to blend DtF and MtA, just go with Gnosticism as the ultimate truth of the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-07-2024, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T17:24:40-08:00","id":1532215,"title":"","content":"Supporting this notion, DtF describes a human's Faith rating as the strength of that person's \u201cspark of divinity\u201d. It has been suggested that, for most people, this is effectively a Sleeping Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T20:25:14-08:00","id":1532226,"title":"","content":"A very interesting idea <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T06:49:58-08:00","id":1532238,"title":"","content":"If Lucifer, or a substantial group of Demons, believe in that (mage Avatars are fragments of God), then the truth of the matter is irrelevant. There will be Demons acting as if it is true. Keeping the actual truth obscure from the Players would probably be wiser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-09-2024, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T15:56:45-08:00","id":1532261,"title":"","content":"I'd also recommend looking at <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/443122/Book-of-the-Damned-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Damned</a>, a bundle of Storyteller's Vault supplements that collectively update DtF's Lores to X20 standards, written by Travis Legge. This will help in crossing DtF over with M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T21:38:10-08:00","id":1532314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532215#post1532215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supporting this notion, DtF describes a human's Faith rating as the strength of that person's \u201cspark of divinity\u201d. It has been suggested that, for most people, this is effectively a Sleeping Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, DtF has that aspect, which curiously align almost perfectly with MtA idea of &quot;Avatars&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm really curious to know if the writers of WoD are secretly Gnostics, or if they took inspiration from it, or if when they were writing the games they simply delved into &quot;occultism&quot; and unknowingly ended up getting their eyes into Gnostic literature... Gnostic cults are a bit secretive, so I recon that many such occultist literature don't just have a label written &quot;those are the Gnostic Gospels&quot;, therefore it isn't much of a stretch that they could have come up with those ideas from Gnostic sources without realizing it.<br /> <br /> Even for VtM there's this touch. I say this because the &quot;God&quot; from VtM sounds an awful like the Gnostic &quot;Demiurge&quot;, the false God that imprisons us in the Material Realm. In fact, and this will be HIGHLY controversial to many, but... One of the reasons that Hitler hated the Jews was that, according to the Nazi lunacy, the Jews were &quot;soulless&quot; - aka, they were created by the Demiurge as beings &quot;made only of this world&quot;, meaning that the Jews were made of matter alone, without the &quot;divine shards&quot;. Which explains why Hitler say nonsensical things like &quot;the only God of Israel is Capital&quot; in his Mein Kampf.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThat all comes from Theosophy, which could be described as a Gnostic Cult. Once you ready Mein Kampf as the &quot;Nazi Bible&quot; instead of some political manifesto, it becomes so much more clear, rather than the incomprehensible babble that he spouts.<br /> <br /> Please, don't hate me... I don't condone any of that nonsense. Now, even if none of you agree with that take, it still remains that those are ideas that are part of the ideas of Theosophy, that some &quot;people&quot; aren't actually people because they don't have &quot;souls&quot; (divine shards), therefore those &quot;people&quot; are servants of the &quot;Demiurge&quot;, beings purely of matter.<br /> <br /> Now, ever since I came to study a bit about Gnosticism (and some other of its &quot;denominations&quot;, like Hermeticism, Theosophy and others, even Masonry of which I had direct contact being a former member), I could no longer ignore how those ideas reassemble the Cainites...<br /> <br /> Think about it... First of all, the God of the Bible is the &quot;Demiurge&quot; (basically, the DEVIL, the jailor of this false prison of illusion which we call as the &quot;material world&quot;).<br /> <br /> Therefore, the one that curses Cain is this Demiurge<br /> <br /> Secondly, Vampires are trapped in this prison... They can't &quot;Ascend&quot;, they have no Avatars and it's even debatable if they still have &quot;souls&quot;.<br /> <br /> They do seen to fit the idea of being the &quot;creatures purely of matter and servants of the Demiurge&quot;.<br /> <br /> What's more, most brands of &quot;Gnosticism&quot; believe in some sort of Reincarnation. And yes, MtA also has Reincarnations as one of its pillars. It goes hand to hand with Gnosticism, which I personally believe that, being that Gnosticism is a very syncretic set of &quot;occult mysticism&quot; rather than a proper religion, I believe that they took these ideas from eastern Buddhism/Hinduism, which seems fitting, considering that Gnosticism comes from the Middle East as a sort of Western+Eastern mix of mystical traditions. Thus, Gnosticism believes that the &quot;divine shards&quot;, given that they are pieces of &quot;God&quot;, they can't really die, and thus they keep reincarnating until they &quot;remember&quot; that they are God. Remember, for Gnosticism this material world and therefore our material bodies is just an illusion cast by the Demiurge to keep us from realizing the truth (that we are all ONE GOD)<br /> <br /> That fits very well for MtA, but Vampires are immortal... Therefore, they don't reincarnate... Therefore, they seem to be very fit in the role of being creatures &quot;created by the Demiurge&quot;, since they are beings purely of the matter and that are incapable to &quot;transcend&quot; (the Gnostic word for transcending the material world and going back to the &quot;pleuma&quot; - the &quot;divine realm&quot;... Don't worry about those silly names), called as &quot;Ascension&quot; in MtA.<br /> <br /> If you do decide to go this route, this creates a very interesting dynamic for all these games, where Lucifer is a saint-like figure, just like the &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot; in real life Hermeticism. The &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot; are those Hermetics that managed to &quot;Transcend&quot; the illusions of the Material World - for the real life Hermetics, Buddha and Jesus are just 2 examples of such &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot;. Thus, those games would basically be a spiritual war against the &quot;Demiurge&quot;, with the &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot; (or maybe we should call them the &quot;Oracles&quot; as per MtA nomenclature) trying to stir the world away from the prison of the material, or in another words, to help humanity to &quot;Ascend&quot;. And Vampires, Fomori, Nephandi and so, probably would be the &quot;Demiurge's spawns&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T06:02:46-07:00","id":1532321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532238#post1532238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lucifer, or a substantial group of Demons, believe in that (mage Avatars are fragments of God), then the truth of the matter is irrelevant. There will be Demons acting as if it is true. Keeping the actual truth obscure from the Players would probably be wiser.</div> </div> </div> </div> The players don't even need to know it at all. That's one of Lucifer's most held secrets, so besides him MAYBE just the Earthbounds are aware of. And some mages &quot;know&quot; this, but I use quotations on the &quot;know&quot; because, in truth, they BELIEVE it.<br /> <br /> Given how the Celestial Chorus is actually the &quot;Western society of Theosophy&quot;, they are the ones that believe in this notion that Avatars are the &quot;fragments of the One&quot;. But that's pretty much &quot;just&quot; a belief system among many others; the fact that (in this scenario) they are the ones who are actually right, is purely coincidental.<br /> <br /> (Also, it's funny how MtA has a group that represents the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the West&quot; in the Celestial Chorus, the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the Middle East&quot; in the Ahl-I-Batin and the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the East&quot; in the Akashics, but it has no groups representing Christianism, Islam or Buddhism, the 3 largest religions in the world. That to me is perhaps the biggest indication of the Gnostic character of the WoD)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T07:23:18-07:00","id":1532376,"title":"","content":"It's not particularly surprising that gnosticism pops up <i>everywhere</i> in pop and counter culture. The broad strokes of gnostisicm - that the creator of the physical world is suspect, that there is wisdom to be found in rebellion and transgression, that a small group of of people are aware of 'the truth,' etc. - are a writer's gold mine. It's a scaffolding for writing stories that feel metaphysically or spiritually deep without actually needing to be deep, and for writing stories without the constraints of more traditional moral systems or lessons. A 'civilians are expendable&quot; mentality doesn't fly in most stories, but with a gnostic framework it becomes the foundation of a cinematic blockbuster, and outside of that same framework the words &quot;there is no spoon&quot; would likely fall flat.<br /> <br /> Gnosticism is also an attractive spiritual or metaphysical framework. In the broad strokes (again) it is dualist, justifies a certain amount of rejection and transgression of mainstream moral and ethical systems, has an understandable answer to questions about the existence of evil, etc. So of course it keeps popping up throughout history in a variety of ways that look broadly similar until you get into their deeper beliefs.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say, I don't think the presence of gnosticism in a modern work, be it the World of Darkness or the Lego Movie, is an indication the writers are well versed in the beliefs of the Gnostics, the Albigensians, or the Theosophists. Some may be, but others are only be passingly familiar with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532321#post1532321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, it's funny how MtA has a group that represents the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the West&quot; in the Celestial Chorus, the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the Middle East&quot; in the Ahl-I-Batin and the &quot;Society of Theosophy of the East&quot; in the Akashics, but it has no groups representing Christianism, Islam or Buddhism, the 3 largest religions in the world. That to me is perhaps the biggest indication of the Gnostic character of the WoD)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its less that the WoD is meant to be deeply gnostic and more that the writers didn't want the vast majority of mages to be Christian, Islamic, or Buddhist, and based on world demographics they probably would be. Having legitimate expressions of those religions in the Traditions would only draw attention to that fact. Instead the game took loose inspiration (stole liberally) from modern secret societies and sects.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect that back in the 90's White Wolf assumed its fanbase would not really want to play a traditional member of a mainstream religion. All that &quot;mages know the real secrets behind your religion&quot; writing wasn't meant as offensive arrogance, it was written for an audience that would find it appealing. It just hasn't aged well.<br /> <br /> Also, also, having legitimate expressions of Christianity, Islam, Buddhism, etc. would mean understanding them well enough to not screw up their beliefs and history and that is harder than it seems. The Wiki page for the messianic voice has them being founded a two to seven years before Christ even started publicly preaching, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T08:20:55-07:00","id":1532437,"title":"","content":"There are many things that overlap between Demon and Mage Lore. Especially Old Mage (where &quot;The One&quot; wasn't just a paradigm thing but the OOC explanation). But not in a single way<br /> <br /> For instance: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pure_Ones_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">The Pure Ones </a>were described as &quot;shards of the One&quot;, but also as independent and &quot;non-human&quot; entities that created the cosmos and it's most basic laws (and also shattered, creating the Avatars).<br /> <br /> The Pure overlap very well with Demons in their role (even if they don't define themselves as &quot;shards&quot;), and this angle was even explored in Demon's own fiction: IIRC, there's a Demon that &quot;sees&quot; a mage using magick, and perceives it as the mutilated &quot;body&quot; of an angel providing the power - the Avatars being dead angels does correlate with them being shards of the Pure, but clashes a little with magick bing purely faith.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, if Angels were &quot;The Pure&quot; that means &quot;the Wyck&quot; (the mythical ancestors of Mages acording to the Verbena <i>and old OOC lore</i>, lore that's still reffered on M20, btw) were half-angels. The Wyck would be what Demon calls the Nephilim. Which doers correlate with Mages being the remanants of the Babel Experiment (as Demon ST handbook suggests), but in a more involved way than what one could fathom from that alone.<br /> <br /> *Then again, when talking about the &quot;truth of the universe&quot;, remember than mages should be allowed to understand it however they want when making Paradigms and such. I would make so there's enough leeway and obscurity to believe, at least, in the &quot;core&quot; philosophies of each major faction.<br /> <br /> Remember that while Demons come integrated with a set of &quot;truths&quot;, these are obscured in the very book trough Demons having lost a lot of memories, and having their very essence warped by the Abyss. So not everything has to align to a T<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, as I see it Mage doesn't place much weight on what the truth is, as long as it can be reinterpreted in many different ways, and as long as &quot;humanity&quot; has - at least potentially - a say about how the world looks like. <hr /><br /> I would recomend to think about how are you going to relate the splats at the level they're going to interact<br /> <br /> *What about The Revelation?, how is that going to work on Mages, taking into account that &quot;belief&quot; it's very important?. The way I handled that it's that Demons look as &quot;something very important and holly&quot; allrigth - but that something it's to be interpretted within Paradigm. it could be Angels, it could be Aliens<br /> <br /> *How does True Magick(tm) affect Demons and their powers?. There's a lot to unpack here, from what Spheres affect Demons to if Faith can be &quot;translated&quot; to Quintessence. One thing that could be very important to make both Demon and Mage antagonists it's wheter mages can destroy, or at least imprission demons. Demons with healty faith networks are very hard to get rid off, so this is going to come out<br /> <br /> *The Umbra it's barely touched on Demon. To the point one can safely ignore al of it but the Dark one. Now you have 3 layers of Penumbra + the DigiWeb + deeper worlds. What do the Demons do with all of this? Maybe the &quot;layers of reality&quot; thing didn't ceased to be, after all, just are on a different place ... Moreover, from a mechanical pov, if Mages are going to actively interact with multiple layers of Otherworlds Demons may want to follow<br /> <br /> Narratively, let's find commonalities (common antagonists, as proposed before, are a good idea):<br /> <br /> *Earthbound are each one a &quot;Cthulhu cult&quot; unto themselves, and one could explore how that interwoves with how mages try to cultivate beliefs in their area<br /> <br /> \u00cef you want to explore <a href=\"https://imgflip.com/m/dnd/tag/the+lore\" target=\"_blank\">The Lore</a>, it also offers interesting things like exploring the remanants of ancient cults and civilizations, that probably had their own magick and inklings on the workings of the cosmos<br /> <br /> *Raveners, some Earthbound, and Nephandi have a lot of overlap in their goals.<br /> <br /> It could also be interesting to think about if the &quot;friendlier&quot; factions of Mages and Demons could share some goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":".  Corrected the meme link to the direct source to alleviate SPAM flag. Please take care when posting links to ensure they're going where intended and not violating any of the forum rules. 03-13-2024, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T15:40:26-07:00","id":1532455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much#post1532080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys. So, Mage: The Ascension bas a lot of demons and they're very different from the protagonists of Demon the Fallen. I wanted to know how to do shared setting between the two games, without changing the setting of either game too much. what is your suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read <i>Demon Storytellers Companion</i> 62-64. It basically explains that when the core speaks of Lucifer teaching humans to wield the secrets of creation and their limitless potential as beings made in the image of God, he means they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mages can drain the 'Faith' out of object and places... which is suggestive of what 'Faith' actually is from a Mage perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T16:33:08-07:00","id":1532460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532080-a-way-for-a-mta-and-dtf-crossover-without-changing-the-lore-if-either-game-too-much?p=1532376#post1532376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not particularly surprising that gnosticism pops up <i>everywhere</i> in pop and counter culture. The broad strokes of gnostisicm - that the creator of the physical world is suspect, that there is wisdom to be found in rebellion and transgression, that a small group of of people are aware of 'the truth,' etc. - are a writer's gold mine. It's a scaffolding for writing stories that feel metaphysically or spiritually deep without actually needing to be deep, and for writing stories without the constraints of more traditional moral systems or lessons. A 'civilians are expendable&quot; mentality doesn't fly in most stories, but with a gnostic framework it becomes the foundation of a cinematic blockbuster, and outside of that same framework the words &quot;there is no spoon&quot; would likely fall flat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Gnosticism is also an attractive spiritual or metaphysical framework. In the broad strokes (again) it is dualist, justifies a certain amount of rejection and transgression of mainstream moral and ethical systems, has an understandable answer to questions about the existence of evil, etc. So of course it keeps popping up throughout history in a variety of ways that look broadly similar until you get into their deeper beliefs.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say, I don't think the presence of gnosticism in a modern work, be it the World of Darkness or the Lego Movie, is an indication the writers are well versed in the beliefs of the Gnostics, the Albigensians, or the Theosophists. Some may be, but others are only be passingly familiar with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Besides, many of these &quot;Gnostic denominations&quot; that have constantly popped out throughout history, be it the first century gnostics proper or the Albigenses or the real world Masons/Rosencruxes, the Luciferans or any other, including the real world Order of Hermes from medieval cults, which all have similar roots and those Gnostic ideas even if each one of these occultist cults have their own particulars, let us call them all &quot;Gnosticism&quot; for simplicity sake, all of these cults delve in the practice of mysticism/occultism, which seems to be a human fascination that draws people in, they are also highly secretive even to this day, which draws even more the curiosity of outsiders, and they hold promises of &quot;secrete knowledge&quot;. &quot;Did you know you've been lied to? &quot;They&quot; don't want you to know the truth&quot;, that's some powerful idea to draw people in, sometimes to their own detriment, when they'll end up brainwashed by some sociopathic cult leaders. It's funny that this is a premisse of the Traditions in Mage lol.<br /> <br /> But, because of their secretive nature, and because of the synthetistic nature of &quot;Gnosticism&quot;, where it just mix and mashes a ton of esoteric into it in different forms, thus constantly &quot;shape shifting&quot; it's core ideas, ranging from the Gnosticism of the first century where the Serpent in the Garden of Even were trying to set Adam and Eve free from the prison of the Demiurge, to the book &quot;Paradise Lost&quot; where Lucifer is the hero fighting a war against the same Demiurge, or the medieval Order of Hermes that has the material world as a good thing, in contrast opposition to &quot;mainstream Gnosticism&quot;, but as a form of &quot;test&quot; that one must overcome in order to reach his true potential (aka remembering that you are God, that part seems to be the common denominator), because of these 2 factors, secretiveness and syncretism, this means that there's no one &quot;Gnostic Bible&quot;, even if there's the 14 books of the &quot;Corpus Hermeticum&quot;, because first of all that's only one of the &quot;denominations&quot; of &quot;Gnosticism&quot;, because no one is completely sure of the authenticity of those, because allegedly they were 16 books, thus 2 are lost to time, and because Hermeticism itself is a collection of vast salad of syncretisms of its time, between the grego-roman, Egyptian and many other pagan religions. And outside Hermeticism, there's also no single, unifying &quot;dogma&quot; in any of these &quot;mystery cults&quot;. There wasn't in Orphism, which is another one of these &quot;mystery cults&quot; at the time of the ancient Greeks, there isn't in contemporary New Age mysticism.<br /> <br /> And thus, what we end up having is that us &quot;normies&quot; stumble from time to time into pieces of esoterica literature that, unknowingly to us, has &quot;Gnostic&quot; roots. &quot;The Law of Attraction&quot;. A recent best seller book. I'm sorry to offend anyone that may read this, but in my opinion that is pure charlathanism. It does however, possess a heavy &quot;Gnostic&quot; influence. That, however, doesn't mean that the writer of it pray to the &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot; in some Illuminati-esque temple trying to achieve the &quot;Astral Plane&quot;. Sure, he could be, but it may just as likely just have absorbed those ideas from culture itself or from &quot;occultist literature&quot;.<br /> <br /> Those Gnostic ideas ARE spread out throughout our culture, and the vast majority of people have no idea about it. I mean, I bet many people tried to press their heads with their hands in order to &quot;wake up&quot; after watching Matrix (or tried to use &quot;the Force&quot; after watching Star Wars), but I doubt that anybody has tried to pray for Hermes Trimeguistus for guidance on how to reach the Astral Plane - I'm using the real world beliefs of the real world OoH here, do not mix those with the game MtA. Real World Order of Hermes have Hermes Trimeguistus as one of their &quot;Masters&quot; - Jesus, Buddha and many others are also their &quot;Masters&quot;, so you see their &quot;syncretism absolutism&quot;, and they believe in several &quot;planes of existence&quot; that one must overcome in order to reach the &quot;Pleuma&quot;, the &quot;divine plane&quot; let us call it. Some of which would be the Ethereal Plane, the Astral Plane and others. So, any time that you hear about &quot;astral projection&quot; in occultist/mysticism circles, know that you are talking about Gnostic/Hermetic ideas that spread out of their secret societies, even if the ones talking about those never heard about Gnosticism or Hermeticism before in their lives.<br /> <br /> Gnostic ideas are even present in &quot;philosophy&quot; and &quot;science&quot; because they &quot;syncretise&quot; everything. Newton was an alchemist and Hegel, the famous German &quot;philosopher&quot; was nothing more nothing less than a Hermetic &quot;wizard&quot; - I'm not joking here. His &quot;Dialects&quot; is just part of what in hermeticism is called &quot;the wizard's circle&quot;, represented by the Greek serpent Ouroboros, which is the symbol of the Hermetic Order, the serpent eating it's own tail (that one the writers of MtA also got right, just open the game's book and you'll see it there). &quot;Dialects&quot; means &quot;embracing contradictions&quot; - thus, if you have A and not-A, instead of saying that one or another is true and the other is false, you embrace BOTH as &quot;A+&quot;. This is Hermeticism straight out of the Corpus Hermeticum. And what is the purpose of it? It's very simple - as I have already explained, the core belief of Gnosticism/Hermeticism is that &quot;individuality&quot; is an illusion, WE ARE ALL GOD and EVERYTHING IS GOD, we just forgot about it, therefore there are NO REAL CONTRADICTIONS, good and evil DO NOT contradict each other, because they are both the same (God). Light and Darkness do NOT contradict each other, for it is all God. And the purpose of Dialectics is to reunite God by embracing contradictions. &quot;Thesis + Antithesis = Synthesis&quot;. Communism + Capitalism = ?? Social Democracy? I don't know.<br /> <br /> For this same reason, Marx claimed to have &quot;demystified Hegel&quot;, so when a Marxist claim to use &quot;Dialectics&quot;, he is in fact &quot;conjuring&quot; a &quot;Hermetic spell&quot; without having the slightest idea. That's how diffused those ideas are within our cultures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think its less that the WoD is meant to be deeply gnostic and more that the writers didn't want the vast majority of mages to be Christian, Islamic, or Buddhist, and based on world demographics they probably would be. Having legitimate expressions of those religions in the Traditions would only draw attention to that fact. Instead the game took loose inspiration (stole liberally) from modern secret societies and sects.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect that back in the 90's White Wolf assumed its fanbase would not really want to play a traditional member of a mainstream religion. All that &quot;mages know the real secrets behind your religion&quot; writing wasn't meant as offensive arrogance, it was written for an audience that would find it appealing. It just hasn't aged well.<br /> <br /> Also, also, having legitimate expressions of Christianity, Islam, Buddhism, etc. would mean understanding them well enough to not screw up their beliefs and history and that is harder than it seems. The Wiki page for the messianic voice has them being founded a two to seven years before Christ even started publicly preaching, for instance. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can understand that reasoning, but that has led to a pretty unrealistic scenario upon which you actually DON'T have a single Mage who is a Christian, or Muslim or Buddhist. Which is absurdly absurd. The exceptions would be the Templars, who are a fringe group of fanatics almost extinct, and the Cabal of the Pure Though, which became utterly atheistic and purged the remaining Christian elements of itself. But Buddhists or Muslims, not a single one. Buddhism and Hinduism by their very natures could be very inductive towards &quot;occultist mages&quot;, while for Islam they could have went with something along the lines of Sufism, but nope, nothing even remotely close. I understand the reasoning, but it's still pretty unrealistic, and that's a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"